# Build context exclusions for `az acr build` / `docker build`.
#
# The API + Web Dockerfiles restore and publish from source in-image, so none of
# the host build outputs are needed in the context. Excluding them cut the ACR
# upload from >1 GB (full tree incl. .terraform provider binaries + stale agent
# worktrees) to a few MB, turning ~18-minute builds into ~2-minute builds.
#
# Keep this list aligned with .gitignore where the intent overlaps; this file
# governs the DOCKER build context specifically (a superset — it also drops
# things that ARE tracked in git but are useless to a container build, e.g.
# infra/, docs/, tests/).

# Version control / IDE
.git
.gitignore
.vs
.vscode
.idea
*.user

# .NET build outputs (Dockerfile runs its own restore/publish)
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.binlog

# Agent worktrees + local tooling state (hundreds of MB of stale bin/obj)
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/

# Infrastructure-as-code (not part of any app image)
infra/
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate*

# Docs, plans, research, thoughts (not shipped in images)
docs/
thoughts/
*.md

# ...EXCEPT the docs the /engineering section embeds as resources
# (PinballWizard.Web.csproj EmbeddedResource entries: the manifest, five named
# top-level docs, and every ADR via docs/adr/*.md). Excluding them strips the
# files from the web build context, so `dotnet publish` fails with CS1566
# "Could not find a part of the path" — the 2026-07-07 web-deploy break.
# These negations MUST follow BOTH `docs/` and `*.md` — later patterns win, and
# `*.md` would otherwise re-exclude the markdown. The `!docs/adr/*.md` glob keeps
# new ADRs working without touching this file again. Only the web Dockerfile
# COPYs docs/, so api/cli/indexer images are unaffected.
!docs/engineering-manifest.json
!docs/*.md
!docs/adr/*.md

# Test projects + fixtures (images build only src/ app projects)
tests/

# Data + eval artifacts
data/eval/results/
tools/

# Node / Playwright
node_modules/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
